{"name":"Mud Puddle","hex":"#9d958b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mednyj Aleut."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of water and soil or fine grained sediment.","A plaster-like mixture used to texture or smooth drywall."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud"},{"term":"puddle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, often temporary, pool of water, usually on a path or road. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Stagnant or polluted water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a puddle.","To play or splash in a puddle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puddle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puddle","blocks":[{"text":"A puddle is a small accumulation of liquid, usually water, on a surface. It can form either by pooling in a depression on the surface, or by surface tension upon a flat surface. Puddles are often characterized by murky water or mud due to the disturbance and dissolving of surrounding sediment, primarily due to precipitation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Begliktash_puddle_%D0%91%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%88_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0_%E2%80%94_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%8F.jpg/330px-Begliktash_puddle_%D0%91%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%88_%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0_%E2%80%94_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%8F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puddle","wikidata":"Q152841"},{"title":"Mud","blocks":[{"text":"Mud is loam, silt, or clay mixed with water. Mud is usually formed after rainfall or near water sources. Ancient mud deposits hardened over geological time to form sedimentary rock such as shale or mudstone. When geological deposits of mud are formed in estuaries, the resultant layers are termed bay muds. Mud has also been used for centuries as a construction resource, mostly for houses, and also as a binder. An Old English word for it was fen, now in most dialects referring to a type of wetland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg/330px-2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud","wikidata":"Q170449"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg/500px-Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg/1280px-Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg/500px-Tadorna_tadorna_%28Tadorne_de_Belon%29_-_363.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A common shelduck drinking from a puddle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATadorna_tadorna_(Tadorne_de_Belon)_-_363.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg/500px-Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg/1280px-Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg/500px-Moisture_and_puddles_on_muddy_road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puddle